From 88a795089fec6f1fbbf04e36ae154fd970a42cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grok Bot <grok-bot@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:42:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] 0.9.2: fix 'Connection errored out' on every action in the
 desktop window

Root cause: desktop.ServerThread imports app.main (builds the Gradio Blocks)
and calls launch() in a worker thread. Gradio 4.44 creates its asyncio
primitives (Queue.pending_message_lock / delete_lock, App.lock / stop_event)
only when asyncio.get_event_loop() works in the constructing thread, and a
non-main thread has no event loop, so they were silently None. Every queued
event then failed in queueing.push (AttributeError: __aenter__) and the
heartbeat stream in routes.stop_stream ('NoneType' object has no attribute
'wait'). The dev start (python app/main.py) builds the UI in the main thread,
which is why it worked there. Package versions are not involved (the same
locked versions work in the main thread), so the lock is unchanged.

- desktop.py: ensure_thread_event_loop() gives the server thread an event
  loop before app.main is imported; after launch check_queue() verifies the
  queue primitives and that the startup events ran, logs "Queue check: OK"
  or a clear QUEUE CHECK FAILED message, and recreates missing primitives.
- verify_runtime.py: a module whose __version__ lookup raises (utils3d's lazy
  attribute loader: "No module named 'utils3d.__version__'") counts as
  working; 0.9.1 setup stopped with a false "MISSING utils3d" and never wrote
  the setup marker.
- tests: test_server_queue.py starts the server exactly like desktop mode
  (app.main built inside ServerThread) and completes a queued event over HTTP
  (/queue/join + /queue/data); the desktop end-to-end test checks the log for
  "Queue check: OK"; verify_runtime lazy-module test.
- Version 0.9.2 (app/version.py, QuokkaForm.iss, README, INSTALL_WINDOWS.txt
  with a note that updating over the top keeps the runtime and models).
